# Add Below: BUT_Add_Click (GCSViews/FlightPlanner.cs:1780-1811), the button to the right of the
# panel's boxes. A blank row - WAYPOINT (16), zeroes, the screen's frame, as Commands_RowsAdded
# leaves one (:2407-2441) - at the end while there is at most one row or the current row is the
# last, and otherwise after the current row; the new row becomes selectedrow (:2472-2475).

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
screen plan
window 1600x1200
budget 6
# A first budget, set by hand until a passing run records one.

expect mission.items 0
click plan-add-below
expect mission.items 1
expect mission.last.command 16
expect mission.last.alt 0
expect mission.frames relative
expect mission.selected 1

# Two waypoints clicked on; with the last row current, Add Below appends.
# The map first: a press before its first paint records nothing.
expect map.ready true
click map@0.40x0.40
click map@0.60x0.40
expect mission.items 3
# Row 3 made current from a known row: the pointer resting on the marker its click just made is
# MainMap_OnMarkerEnter on Windows, which reports it, and puts the grid on row 3 already
# (FlightPlanner.cs:8065-8095) - where X11 sends no motion for a still pointer - and a click on
# the current row clears it. Row 2 first, from either.
click plan-row-2
expect mission.selected 2
click plan-row-3
expect mission.selected 3
click plan-add-below
expect mission.items 4
expect mission.selected 4
expect mission.last.alt 0

# With the first row current, the new row goes second: the last row is still a blank one.
click plan-row-1
click plan-add-below
expect mission.items 5
expect mission.selected 2
expect mission.last.alt 0
expect mission.commands 16,16,16,16,16
